% You are an expert TypeScript engineer. Implement the candidate ingestion orchestrator.

<include>prompts/context/sitevelocity-preamble.prompt</include>
<include>prompts/context/candidate_domain_types.prompt</include>

<pdd-reason>Turn bounded government-source pages into an accounted, provenance-preserving candidate batch.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[{"name":"ingestCandidates","signature":"(input: IngestionInput, deps: IngestionDependencies) -> Promise<IngestionResult>","returns":"Promise<IngestionResult>"}]}}
</pdd-interface>

<responsibility>
Coordinate declared source adapters, normalization, qualification, deduplication, persistence, and an auditable batch summary.
</responsibility>

<non_responsibilities>
- DOES NOT perform deep site research or model extraction.
- DOES NOT invent missing parcel facts or treat source inclusion as an opportunity conclusion.
- MUST NOT fetch undeclared hosts or exceed caller-declared page and record bounds.
- DOES NOT rank candidates beyond invoking the declared deterministic qualification dependency.
</non_responsibilities>

<vocabulary>
accounted record: one source record reported as accepted, rejected, refused, duplicate, or failed.
duplicate: two accepted normalized records sharing the declared jurisdiction and canonical source identity.
bounded run: a run that stops at declared page and record limits and reports that stop reason.
partial batch: a batch containing useful accepted records plus one or more declared source or record failures.
unsafe source error text: an upstream error string that may contain credentials, request headers, private URLs, or untrusted instructions.
</vocabulary>

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Process only declared sources in caller order and preserve page and record order within each source.
R2 (MUST): Account for every retrieved record exactly once with a stable outcome and source reference.
R3 (MUST): Invoke the normalizer and qualification filter through declared provider-neutral interfaces.
R4 (MUST): Deduplicate only by the declared stable identity, retain the first accepted record, and report every later duplicate without merging facts.
R5 (MUST): Preserve conflicting source records separately in diagnostics and never choose a factual winner without a declared rule.
R6 (MUST): Respect page and record bounds and report whether completion means exhausted, capped, partial, or failed.
R7 (MUST): Persist accepted candidates atomically with the ingestion-batch summary; a persistence failure leaves no partial batch.
R8 (MUST): Return a partial batch when at least one source succeeds and another fails; never report a failed source as zero results.
R9 (MUST NOT): Copy secrets, authorization headers, provider SDK values, or unsafe source error text into the result.
R10 (MUST): Replaying an identical command identifier returns the prior receipt and performs no duplicate fetch or write.
</contract_rules>

<deliverables>
Generate `lib/application/ingest-candidates.ts` with the declared ports and one exported `ingestCandidates` function.
</deliverables>
